BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-lx40q6@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T000100
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T020100
SUMMARY:Beyond Henson: Puppetry and World Cinema
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by the work of The Jim Henson Company and Jim Henson
 ’s Creature Shop\, the film program ‘Beyond Henson: Puppetry and World
  Cinema’ surveys the rich international history of storytelling through 
 the artforms of cinema and puppetry. Presented in conjunction with the ‘
 Make\, Believe\, Magic: The Worlds of The Jim Henson Company’ exhibition
  (12 September 2026 – 18 April 2027)\, the film program delves into craf
 ted narratives that harness traditions of puppetry and cinema to move beyo
 nd belief and into the realms of the imagination. To trace the anatomy of 
 onscreen puppetry is to draw from millennia of performance and craft tradi
 tions that extend across the globe. From the marionette puppetry of France
  and the Bunraku theatre of Japan\, to the Wayang Kulit puppetry of Indone
 sia and the British Punch and Judy show\, the democratised nature of the p
 uppet theatre has enabled an unbridled style of performance that can enact
  the truthful and the taboo. Taking direction from the television series J
 im Henson Presents the World of Puppetry 1985\, the selected titles includ
 e films that precede (and sit adjacent to) productions by The Jim Henson C
 ompany\, positioning the Company’s work within the broader canon of on-s
 creen puppetry. [sponsorLogos block] QAGOMA acknowledges the generous assi
 stance of the National Film and Sound Archive of Australia\, Canberra\; th
 e Academy Film Archive\, Los Angeles\; the British Film Institute\, London
 \; the NBCUniversal Archives & Collections\, Los Angeles\; the Library of 
 Congress\, Washington\; the National Film Archive\, Prague\, the Australia
 n Film Television and Radio School\, Sydney and the Revival House\, Perth 
 in providing materials for this program. Program curated by Victoria Wareh
 am\, Australian Cinémathèque with additional film note writing by Rebeka
 h Brammer.
LOCATION:GOMA\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/cinema/program/beyond-henson-puppetry-and
 -world-cinema
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:brisbane-ielqa9@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T000100
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260912T020100
SUMMARY:Where the Wild Things Are Made: Jim Henson’s Creature Shop
DESCRIPTION:Presented alongside the ‘Make\, Believe\, Magic: The Worlds o
 f The Jim Henson Company’ special exhibition (12 September 2026 – 18 A
 pril 2027)\, ‘Where the Wild Things Are Made: Jim Henson’s Creature Sh
 op’ celebrates the skill and craftsmanship of the artisans at Jim Henson
 ’s Creature Shop. Highlighting the diverse portfolio of expressive chara
 cters and creatures made by the Company for external productions\, the sel
 ected films showcase the work of Jim Henson’s Creature Shop and how it c
 ontinues to shape the landscape of cinematic storytelling. An important fa
 cet of The Jim Henson Company\, Jim Henson’s Creature Shop is internatio
 nally renowned for creating pioneering techniques that bring extraordinary
  characters and stories to life. Formally established following the releas
 e of Labyrinth in 1986\, Jim Henson’s Creature Shop continues to be an e
 nduring creative hub where performance and craftsmanship is paired with ex
 perimentation and ground-breaking technical innovation to transform the im
 aginary into reality. [sponsorLogos block] QAGOMA acknowledges the generou
 s assistance of the National Film and Sound Archive of Australia\, Canberr
 a\; the Norwegian Film Institute\, Oslo and the Revival House\, Perth in p
 roviding materials for this program. Program curated by Victoria Wareham\,
  Australian Cinémathèque with additional film note writing by Rebekah Br
 ammer.
LOCATION:GOMA\, Stanley Place\, South Bank
URL:https://www.qagoma.qld.gov.au/cinema/program/where-the-wild-things-are-
 made-jim-hensons-creature-shop
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
